cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Phytotron, please cite it as below."
title: "Phytotron: an open virtual phytotron for benchmarking greenhouse climate control"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Growmatics B.V."
    country: NL
    website: "https://growmatics.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/growmatics/phytotron"
url: "https://growmatics.ai/phytotron"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-11"
keywords:
  - greenhouse climate control
  - benchmark
  - model predictive control
  - reinforcement learning
  - tomato
  - crop safety
abstract: >-
  Phytotron is an open, simulated benchmark for greenhouse climate control. Controllers
  run through the same simulated tomato seasons (GreenLight model via GreenLight-Gym2),
  are checked against crop-safety rules taken from published horticultural sources, and
  only then are compared on net economic value and decision time. All results are
  simulated.
